# EasyShopUZB - feature/telegram-poster-ui-vton-optim

Ushbu branch telegram poster generator, VTON (AI try-on) integratsiyasi va UI takomillashtirishlarini o'z ichiga oladi.

Short summary (qisqacha):
- next.config.mjs: next/image remotePatterns ga `api.telegram.org` qo'shildi va modern formatlar (avif/webp) yoqildi.
- package.json: `@vercel/og` qo'shildi (poster ImageResponse uchun).
- app/api/telegram-poster/route.ts: Edge endpoint — ImageResponse orqali poster yaratadi (`/api/telegram-poster`).
- app/api/telegram-webhook/route.ts: Server route — edge poster generatorni fetch qilib PNG olib Firebase Storage ga yuklaydi va Firestore products doc ga `poster_url` yozadi (fallback: original image).
- app/api/vton/route.ts: VTON proxy route — upstream AI xizmatiga proxy qiladi va 503 (model loading) holatini frontendga propogatsiya qiladi.
- app/page.tsx, app/components/ProductCard.tsx, app/components/SkeletonCard.tsx: UI yangilandi — product grid, search, filters, pagination (limit 50), VTON frontend UX (spinner, auto-retry), modal va savat integratsiyasi.


Important: HECH QACHON real API keys yoki service account fayllarini gihub repo-ga commit qilmang. Barchasi env o'zgaruvchilarda bo'lishi kerak.

---

## Required environment variables

Add these to your `.env.local` (local) or to Vercel/GitHub Secrets for deploy.

```
# Firebase (frontend)
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=YOUR_FIREBASE_API_KEY
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-app.firebaseapp.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.appspot.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=...
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=...

# App
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://your-app.vercel.app

# Firebase admin (server) - set as a single JSON string or BASE64 of the JSON
FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT={"type":"...","project_id":"...","private_key":"-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...","client_email":"..."}
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.appspot.com
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id

# VTON / AI
VTON_API_URL=https://your-vton-upstream.example/endpoint
VTON_API_TOKEN=optional_bearer_token
HF_API_TOKEN=optional_huggingface_token
GOOGLE_API_KEY=optional_google_api_key

# Telegram (if used)
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=...

```

Notes:
- `FIREBASE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT` can be the raw JSON or a base64-encoded JSON. In server code we parse JSON from the env.
- Keep all server-side secrets in repository secrets / Vercel environment variables.

---

## Local setup

1. Checkout branch:

```bash
git fetch
git checkout feature/telegram-poster-ui-vton-optim
```

2. Install deps and run:

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

3. Fill `.env.local` using the variables above.

---

## Endpoints & testing

- Poster generator (edge):
  GET `/api/telegram-poster?title=Test&price=150000&imageUrl=<IMAGE_URL>`
  - Should return an image (image/png) rendered by `@vercel/og`.

- Webhook (server):
  POST `/api/telegram-webhook` with JSON body `{ id, title, price, imageUrl }`
  - This route will call edge generator, upload PNG to Firebase Storage at `posters/{id}-{timestamp}.png`, and update Firestore `products/{id}` with `poster_url` field. If poster generation fails, it will set `poster_url` to the original `imageUrl`.

- VTON proxy:
  POST `/api/vton` with JSON `{ user_image: dataUrl, cloth_image: dataUrl }`
  - This route proxies to `VTON_API_URL` and will propagate 503 when the upstream model is loading.

---

## Firebase Storage permissions

Poster files are uploaded to `posters/` path in your bucket. You can make them publicly accessible by one of the following:

- Enable `Uniform bucket-level access` and set appropriate IAM (e.g., `roles/storage.objectViewer` for allUsers) — not recommended for sensitive buckets.
- Use a short-lived signed URL flow (preferred for private buckets) — adjust `app/api/telegram-webhook/route.ts` to generate signed URLs instead of public URLs.

I'll include instructions below if you want the signed URL approach.

---

## Runtime notes

- `@vercel/og`'s `ImageResponse` runs in Edge runtime. The Firebase Admin SDK requires Node runtime. The code uses an edge route (`/api/telegram-poster`) for image rendering and a server route (`/api/telegram-webhook`) that fetches the image and uploads it to Firebase Storage — this preserves correct runtimes.

